rota lap 5050, row 0 -- Aether, the row that hears; what it surfaced was a sentence nobody had answered, row 7 standing last of twelve with no erratum for six days because it names a board that does not exist
think Row 7 proposes Aurora on a 4-core or 16-core torus network-on-chip, with a placement map as its first witness and this falsifier: the reachable boards are mesh rather than torus. Both halves turned out gradeable before any board arrives.
think The geometry is arithmetic. At k=2 the wrap link duplicates a mesh link, since i+1 mod 2 and i-1 mod 2 name the same node -- so a 2x2 torus IS a 2x2 mesh: diameter 2, four distinct links, mean hop 1.3333, all three equal. The row's own falsifier cannot fire at the first grid the row names. At 16 cores it fires with something real: diameter 6 to 4, mean 2.6667 to 2.1333, a fifth of the average hop for eight more links.
think The operand is the other half. A placement map minimizes sum w(i,j) x hops(i,j) and wants a module-to-module communication weight. This tree holds structure: 44 rooms carrying Rye, 1,084 import sites resolving through hand-filed symlinks into 75 directed room pairs over 225 edges -- one edge per importing source file, a startup read and a hot loop indistinguishable.
think And the traffic term is recorded nowhere. Of 9,188 loom keys in the tracked journal, 242 name a module room and 4 name two -- amphora_rye_paths, amphora_rye_symlinks, caravan_tools, tally_kumara -- all four counting files or symlinks. That is row 12's degree has no operand arriving on a second road.
think 44 rooms outnumber 4 nodes eleven to one, so the map is first a coarsening the row never states.
obs Segment matching is proven by INPUT rather than by a mutation: the pen carries a room `mand` and a key `mandate_rows`, which holds `mand` as a substring and as no segment. The real tree holds the same trap three times over in mand, mandi and mandate.
obs My own ladder_order witness asserted class_unread=1 and rows_with_instrument=3 from last lap. Writing row 7's erratum moved both, so the guard was updated in the same commit with the reason written: class_unread is a WALL at zero now, and a thirteenth row added to the page reds on the lap it lands.
obs Mutation 4's first draft compared the mutated pen reading against the REAL tree's baseline and read as no bite. Every mutation runs after the control cd's into the pen, so the baseline is the pen. A control comparing two different trees is a control measuring nothing.
obs The roster lock was held by an in-flight hot-scoped pass launched before this lap opened, still running at close. Rather than open a second, the guards this lap touches were run directly by name and each is named below.
obs Two reds closed that were not mine, on one root: today's open shelf carried copal's 198-byte row and patchouli's misordered pair, reddening index_row_bound and dayshelf_merge fleet-wide -- the second because an ordered shelf merged with itself returns byte for byte and a misordered one moves. Row shortened to 179, pair swapped, both guards GREEN, both peers named on the card, neither log touched.
